  "description": "<p>At present fedora supports setting premis:hasSize in an attempt to allow external binaries where fedora either cannot or should not retrieve the external content in order to determine the size of the file. This <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-4096\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">allowance is problematic and produces unexpected outcomes</a>, and is not scoped to external binaries. </p>\n\n<p>In order to scope this allowance exclusively to external binaries, we should introduce a \"size\" parameter to the ExternalContent Link header supplied during creation/update.  Custom params should be allowed by the spec, and we in fact already require one custom param, “handling”. Here is an example with the new size param:</p>\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>curl -i -H\"Link: &lt;file:///local/file/storage/wonderful.tiff&gt;; rel=\\\"http://fedora.info/definitions/fcrepo#ExternalContent\\\\\"; handling=\\\"proxy\\\"; type=\\\"image/tiff\\\"; size=\\\"6551596\\\"\" -XPUT -ufedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin http://localhost:8080/rest/test_proxy</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n<p>We would set the fcrepo size header for the binary from this value. That is used to set Content-Size and premis:hasSize/premis3:size in responses. If its not supplied, then the size would be set with existing behaviors.</p>\n\n<p>This may be considered a new feature, and as such would target a minor release.</p>",
